.TH DCC-FAN-CLI 1 2026-11-27 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc-fan-cli \- show and set the notebook fan speed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcc-fan-cli
.br
.B dcc-fan-cli \-\-set
.I percent
.br
.B dcc-fan-cli \-\-auto
.br
.B dcc-fan-cli \-\-log\-level
.I level
.br
.B dcc-fan-cli \-\-log\-level\-get
.br
.B dcc-fan-cli \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without options,
.B dcc-fan-cli
shows the CPU and GPU temperatures, the speed of both fans (duty in percent
and measured RPM) and, while an NVIDIA or AMD GPU is awake, its power, clock
and load (a powered-down GPU is not woken up).
.PP
The status display,
.B \-\-set
and
.B \-\-auto
read and write the embedded controller (EC).
With the
.BR dcc_fan (4)
module loaded they go through it, and the status needs no root; otherwise
they use the I/O ports directly, which needs root and the administrator's
opt-in
.RB ( "dcc-component ec-direct enable" ,
see
.BR dcc-component (8)),
and only if the EC answers like a Clevo EC.
Without EC access the status shows the CPU temperature from coretemp, k10temp
or zenpower and the reason, and
.B \-\-set
and
.B \-\-auto
fail.
Setting the speed always needs root.
The status names the method (\(lqEC access\(rq).
.B \-\-log\-level
and
.B \-\-log\-level\-get
talk to
.BR dcc-fan-daemon (8)
and need membership in the group
.BR dudes-control-center .
.PP
For normal use, choose fan curves and fixed speeds in
.BR dcc-gui (1);
the daemon then keeps them across reboots and applies its safety checks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-set " percent"
Set both fans to a fixed duty: 0, 10, 20, ... 100 (0 switches the fans off).
While
.BR dcc-fan-daemon (8)
runs, it overwrites this value at its next control step; the daemon's
service uses
.B \-\-set 100
as its fail-safe when it stops.
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Run a simple built-in temperature control in the foreground until
.B Ctrl+C .
Invalid CPU temperatures set the fans to 100\~%.
Stop
.B dcc-fan-daemon
first, otherwise both write to the EC.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
Set the daemon's log level:
.BR ERROR ", " WARN ", " INFO " or " DEBUG .
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level\-get
Show the daemon's log level.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show a short help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error (no EC access, daemon not reachable, invalid
value).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sudo dcc-fan-cli
Show temperatures and fans.
.TP
.B dcc-fan-cli \-\-log\-level DEBUG
Let the daemon log every control step.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-fan-daemon (8),
.BR dcc_fan (4),
.BR dcc-gui (1)
